  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD supporting Drought Emergency Response &amp; recovery in Marsabit &amp; Isiolo 2017</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">After the devastating drought of 2016/17 and the emergency response in Isiolo &amp; Marsabit, the communities are still vulnerable and there is need for continuous support to make sure that they recover and their resilience is strengthened to enable them cope with future droughts.   The prolonged drought in the region resulted in water &amp; pasture shortages, food insecurity situation and worsening health &amp; nutrition status of vulnerable people.  
CAFOD Nairobi Office through  DEC and CAFOD appeal funding supported Isiolo &amp; Marsabit in Phase 1 of this project.  This is phase 2 of the same project where CAFOD will support the same partners for a period of 12months. In this phase CAFOD will support partners through facilitation of grant start-up project, carry out a research comparing 2011 and 2017 responses, documenting lessons learnt, timeliness, perceptions and perspectives on how stakeholders responded, facilitate half yearly review and planning meetings (peer review, process review and identify milestones).</narrative>
  </description>
